# blood-brain: Blood's tuned version of qwen3:4b-instruct
#
# A Modelfile is a small recipe: "take this model and change these settings".
# It reuses the same model file (no download). Create or update it with:
#     ollama create blood-brain -f tools\blood-brain.Modelfile
# Then pick "blood-brain" as the model in Home Assistant's Ollama agent.
# Undo: pick qwen3:4b-instruct again (and optionally: ollama rm blood-brain).
#
# Why: Home Assistant's Ollama integration can't set these, so we bake them in.
# Tested with tests/blood_bench.py (see docs/tutorial/04).

FROM qwen3:4b-instruct

# Put ALL layers on the graphics card. Ollama's own guess left ~27% on the slow CPU.
# Measured on the bench: 1.4 s per answer instead of 3.4 s. Uses ~3.4 GB of the 4 GB card,
# so quit Ollama (tray icon → Quit) before running games or other GPU-heavy apps.
PARAMETER num_gpu 99

# Answer-length cap. Without it, the model once wrote 6,000+ words in a loop,
# which would hang Blood for minutes. 400 tokens is plenty for spoken answers.
PARAMETER num_predict 400

# Less random word choice (default 0.7). Same test score, steadier behaviour.
PARAMETER temperature 0.2

# Same as the agent's Context window size in Home Assistant (chapter 04).
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
